<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-SECOND SUPER-G SCHEDULED FOR GARMISCH.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SECOND SUPER-G SCHEDULED FOR GARMISCH.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Alpine skiing World Cup continued to juggle its schedule on Thursday adding a second men's super-G to the programme of races in Garmisch-Partenkirchen, Germany next month.</p>
<p>The German resort will kick off a weekend of racing on February 21 with the super-G that was orginally secheduled for December 8 at the Canadian resort of Whistler.</p>
<p>The race will be followed by a downhill and another super-G.</p>
</text>
